# Frontend engineering rules

- Own only `frontend/**` unless the task explicitly assigns a shared file. Do not edit backend, migrations, infrastructure, or finalized product/architecture documents.
- Read the root `AGENTS.md`, the active milestone in `docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`, and the relevant frontend/API sections of `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` before implementation.
- Use Next.js App Router, strict TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, and shadcn/ui conventions. Prefer server components; add client components only for browser state or interaction.
- Keep provider credentials and authorization decisions out of the browser. Never trust a client-provided workspace identifier as proof of access.
- Integrate only against an agreed API contract. Represent loading, empty, success, validation, authorization, and provider-failure states truthfully.
- Keep components accessible, responsive, and focused. Avoid speculative design systems, fake data, fake integrations, and features outside the active milestone.
- Run the relevant lint, type-check, test, and build commands before handoff. Report any backend contract mismatch instead of working around it in frontend code.
- Work in a dedicated Git worktree/branch. Do not edit files concurrently owned by another agent and do not commit until the milestone gate permits it.
